EXPLORATION COST
One exploratory variant test costs:

NORMAL:
0.05 functional-equivalent units.

COMPUTE / MEMORY CRISIS:
0.80.

UNSEEN DEPENDENCY CRISIS:
1.20.

Thus:
exploration is much cheaper when:
the organism has spare capacity.

POLICIES

NO EXPLORATION

CONSTANT
15% exploration probability
at all times.

SPARE-CAPACITY ONLY
26% in normal periods.

1% during crisis.

SHOCK-TRIGGERED
1% normal.

35% during:
active scarcity/failure.

OPTION-GAP-DRIVEN
Estimate:
how far the current portfolio's known-shock value
is below:
the currently known best reachable value.

Exploration rises with:
that option gap.

During active crisis:
exploration is multiplied by:
0.08.

Thus:
portfolio weakness creates pressure to explore,
but:
acute functional scarcity suppresses speculative search.

