PRIMARY OPTION-GAP RESULT
The option-gap policy achieves:
the highest tested total reward

while using:

approximately 43%
fewer exploration actions
than:
spare-capacity-only.

It also produces:
the best tested unseen dependency-failure reward.

The policy explores:
because:
the current future portfolio is weak,

not merely because:
time passed
or
a shock occurred.

GENERAL PRINCIPLE
EXPLORE WHEN:

OPTION COVERAGE IS LOW

AND

THE MARGINAL COST OF EXPLORATION IS LOW.

Suppress exploration when:

ACTIVE SURVIVAL / REPAIR COST
IS HIGH.

This makes:
evolvability

a dynamically priced:
metabolic process.

RELATION TO H26 / H55
H26:
slow structural adaptation needs:
minimum access
without monopolizing crisis resources.

H55:
repair can dominate acute resource allocation
while:
slow learning retains bounded access.

H87:
cryptic exploration should follow:
the same resource hierarchy.

Exploration is:
important,
but not:
urgent repair.

RELATION TO H85-H86
H85:
neutral variation creates options.

H86:
memory chooses:
which options to preserve.

H87:
metabolism decides:
when to generate new options.

Together:

GENERATE
->
VALIDATE
->
SELECT
->
STORE

becomes:
a complete option-development lifecycle.

OUTSIDE-STATUS-QUO IMPLICATION
A developmental intelligence may use:
periods of low external pressure

to deliberately expand:
its repertoire of function-preserving internal variants.

The variants need not:
improve current performance.

They can be justified by:
future reachability.

This resembles:
preventive developmental experimentation

rather than:
ordinary reward maximization.

DECISION
AR-H87 is POSITIVE WITH A CRISIS-EXPLORATION FAILURE.

Supported synthetically:

- neutral exploration has measurable current cost and future value;
- constant exploration improves robustness but wastes expensive crisis resource;
- spare-capacity exploration performs better;
- shock-triggered exploration is too late for early shock protection;
- option-gap-driven exploration reaches similar/better future coverage with fewer exploratory actions;
- unseen failure performance improves when cryptic options are prepared before the shock;
- evolvability can be treated as a dynamically budgeted process.

Not demonstrated:

- safe real program-variant generation;
- real option-gap estimator;
- real neutral equivalence validation cost;
- long-term lineage inheritance;
- interaction with sleep/dormancy;
- relationship to semantic intelligence.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
AR-H88 — ENDOGENOUS FUNCTIONAL CREDIT WITHOUT EXPLICIT TERMINAL TASK REWARD

